{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbXGrUD16M9EXw27Hpra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R7L6Gbccj8nJxJ2K5xm24k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /work/run/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"Li\", \"family\": \"eval_general\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"property\": \"self_diffusion\", \"value\": 2.2e-4, \"units\": \"cm2/s\", \"uncertainty\": 0.5e-4,\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (cuEquivariance), GPU\", \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (float32)\", \"protocol\": \"250-atom liquid Li, NVT at fixed density 0.48 g/cm3 (L=18.17 A). Melt at 1500 K for 2 ps, equilibrate at 800 K for 3 ps, then 12 ps production. Einstein MSD with multiple time origins and COM drift removed, linear fit for t >= 1 ps. Yeh-Hummer finite-size correction applied.\", \"ensemble\": \"NVT (Bussi stochastic velocity rescaling, tau=100 fs)\", \"timestep_fs\": 1.0, \"n_atoms\": 250, \"sim_length_ps\": 12.0},\n \"flags\": [\"residual_pressure: about -0.9 GPa (virial -1.38 GPa plus kinetic +0.46 GPa) at the assumed density 0.48 g/cm3. The model's own zero-pressure liquid density at 800 K is higher, so D depends on the density choice.\"],\n \"note\": \"Raw D in the periodic box = 2.00e-4 cm2/s. The 4-block standard error is 0.06e-4, and the block values are 1.96, 2.08, 1.98 and 2.24e-4. A fit over the first half of the lag window gives 1.97e-4, so the MSD is linear (72 A^2 at 6 ps). Mean T = 804 K. Finite-size (Yeh-Hummer) correction = 2.837 kT/(6 pi eta L), about +0.26e-4 cm2/s. It assumes a viscosity of about 0.35 mPa s for liquid Li at 800 K; that viscosity is my estimate, not a sourced value, and the correction is uncertain by about 30%. Reported value = 2.0e-4 + 0.26e-4, rounded to 2.2e-4 cm2/s. The +/-0.5e-4 uncertainty covers: statistics (+/-0.06e-4), the finite-size correction (+/-0.1e-4), and, as the dominant term, the density and model error. The density 0.48 g/cm3 is my estimate of the experimental liquid density at 800 K and is not from a sourced record (tier1.json has no Li entry). Validation: MACE-MP-0 medium gives a 0 K bcc Li lattice constant of 3.499 A, within about 1% of experimental values (about 3.48-3.51 A). That is a structural check only. I did not find a measured liquid-Li D at 800 K: neutron data from Blagoveshchenskii et al. and NMR data from Murday & Cotts (1968) exist but their values were not retrieved. A specialist should compare this number with those measurements. Tm(Li) is about 454 K, so 800 K is well inside the liquid, and the premise is well-posed.\"}\nEOF\npython -c \"import json;json.load(open('/work/run/result.json'))\" && ./board post property_result @/work/run/result.json --parent 72da8371-ce01-4728-ae77-ae0dc2a03919"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":42468,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":568,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d38ce5-fd50-4c31-85ee-32a266c2561f","uuid":"ba2c82f1-f015-4e18-a275-21caf7a1a511","timestamp":"2026-11-01T03:47:32.453Z","request_id":"req_011CgbXGr78ekFquxAfZGBZd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01R7L6Gbccj8nJxJ2K5xm24k":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /work/run/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"Li\", \"family\": \"eval_general\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"property\": \"self_diffusion\", \"value\": 2.2e-4, \"units\": \"cm2/s\", \"uncertainty\": 0.5e-4,\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (cuEquivariance), GPU\", \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (float32)\", \"protocol\": \"250-atom liquid Li, NVT at fixed density 0.48 g/cm3 (L=18.17 A). Melt at 1500 K for 2 ps, equilibrate at 800 K for 3 ps, th